\ Spitfire: the countryside near the aircraft. The land within 3 km is
\ divided by hedges into irregular four-sided fields of about 6 to 20
\ hectares, the hedges running between corners scattered about a 250 m
\ lattice, some left out, some planted as lines of trees, trees standing in
\ others, and now and then a farm, a house and a barn about a yard; lanes
\ follow the hedges' lines from one kilometre to the next. The layout comes
\ from a hash of each corner's and hedge's position, so the same fields are there
\ whenever the aircraft returns. In Norway the fields lie only on the level
\ farmland below 150 m, without hedges or lanes, white under the snow, with
\ a red barn and a white house about many of the yards; the ground above
\ them is the terrain's own forest, heath, rock and snow. A kilometre of
\ water has ripples instead,
\ short strokes on the surface, more of them next to an aircraft below 400 m.
\ Kilometres within reach of a town or an airfield are left clear for their
\ own buildings; a town's ground is filled grey or brown in squares of
\ 350 m out to an irregular edge, its parks green, built once. The objects of the kilometres near the aircraft are kept and
\ gathered again only when the aircraft crosses into another kilometre or
\ through 400 m.

3 constant countryside-reach

variable countryside-objects
{ } to countryside-objects
variable countryside-collection
{ :objects [ ] :centres 0 4 0-matrix :radii 0 1 0-matrix } to countryside-collection
\ the near kilometres' field meshes, their centres and radii for culling, and the centres of the grid tiles they lie on
variable countryside-fields
{ :meshes [ ] :centres 0 4 0-matrix :radii 0 1 0-matrix :tile-centres 0 4 0-matrix } to countryside-fields
variable countryside-cell
[ null null ] to countryside-cell

\ the places whose surroundings stay clear of fields, with how far
[ [ :edinburgh-castle 3500 ] [ :leith 1500 ] [ :glasgow-cathedral 4500 ] [ :govan 2000 ] [ :clydebank 1500 ]
  [ :inverness-castle 2000 ] [ :stirling-castle 1500 ] [ :turnhouse 1200 ] [ :drem 1200 ]
  [ :abbotsinch 1200 ] [ :dalcross 1200 ] [ :nidaros 1500 ] [ :vaernes 1200 ]
  [ :marischal-college 2500 ] [ :peterhead 1000 ] [ :montrose 1000 ] [ :kirkwall 1000 ] [ :lerwick 800 ]
  [ :hatston 1200 ] [ :skeabrae 1200 ] [ :castletown 1200 ] [ :sumburgh 1200 ] [ :montrose-air-station 1200 ]
  [ :dyce 1200 ] [ :wick 1200 ] ] to clear-places

\ whether a kilometre's centre lies within a clear place's reach
: clear-cell? ( x z -- flag )
	| x z |
	clear-places ( place |
		place first landmark-ground to centre
		centre first x - sq centre 2 @i z - sq + sqrt place second <
	) any? ;

0x8c8878 constant road-colour

\ a kilometre of water's ripples: strokes 60 m long running east and west, those that fall on water; null when none does
: ripples ( column row n-strokes -- object )
	| column row n-strokes |
	land-origin-x column land-cell * + to west
	land-origin-z row land-cell * + to south
	column 7.31 * row 13.17 * + to seed
	new-sketch to waves
	0 to n-drawn
	0 n-strokes 1 do k
		seed k 2.3 * + hash-fraction land-cell * west + to x
		seed k 4.7 * + 0.5 + hash-fraction land-cell * south + to z
		x z water-at? if
			waves [ [ x 30 - 0 z ] [ x 30 + 0 z ] ] sketch-path
			++ n-drawn
		then
	loop
	n-drawn 0 = if null exit then
	waves bank-colour sketch>object ;

\ a line along the ground at sea level, a point every 100 m, so it can follow the ground once lifted
: ground-line ( sketch from onto coastal -- )
	| sketch from onto coastal |
	onto from v- v-length 100 / round-up 1 max2 to n-pieces
	[ 0 n-pieces 1+ 1 do k from onto k n-pieces / v-between loop ] to points
	coastal not if sketch points sketch-path exit then
	[ ] to run
	0 points size 1+ 1 do k
		k points size < if points k @i to point point first point 2 @i water-at? not else false then if
			run point add-last! drop
		else
			run size 1 > if sketch run sketch-path then
			[ ] to run
		then
	loop ;

\ whether a kilometre touches the water: any of its corners, the middles of its sides or its centre on water
: coastal-cell? ( west south -- flag )
	| west south |
	[ 0 0.5 1 ] ( across | [ 0 0.5 1 ] ( along | west across land-cell * + south along land-cell * + water-at? ) map ) map flatten ( wet | wet ) any? ;

\ a sketch's points raised by the ground's height under them, from the hill cones given and the terrain
: lift-sketch ( sketch cones -- )
	| sketch cones |
	sketch sketch@points ( point | [ point first point second point first point 2 @i cones ground-height-under + point 2 @i ] ) map :points ! drop ;

\ the hill cones that may stand under a kilometre, and whether the kilometre needs lifting at all: a cone near it, or one of the terrain's grids round it
: cell-cones ( west south -- cones lift )
	| west south |
	west land-cell 2 / + to centre-x
	south land-cell 2 / + to centre-z
	hill-cones ( cone | cone first centre-x - sq cone second centre-z - sq + sqrt cone 2 @i land-cell + < ) filter to near
	near
	near size 0 >
	terrain-grids ( grid | centre-x centre-z grid land-cell near-grid? ) any? or ;

\ === the fields ===

\ the hedges' corners every 250 m on a lattice laid from the countryside's origin, four to a kilometre each way, each moved off its place by up to 35% of the spacing either way by a hash of its place, so the fields are four-sided but no two alike and no hedge runs straight for long; of the hedges between neighbouring corners three in ten left out, joining fields into bigger ones, about 6 to 20 hectares, and of those kept about one in eight planted as a line of trees instead; one lattice line in twenty, east and west or north and south, carrying a lane 6 m wide in place of its hedges, about one every 5 km as before (the spacing, the shares and the widths estimates)
250 constant hedge-spacing
0.35 constant corner-shift
0.3 constant hedge-gap-share
0.12 constant tree-line-share
0.05 constant lane-share
0x3e5a2c constant hedge-colour

\ a corner of the hedges, [ x 0 z ], by its place on the lattice
: hedge-corner ( lattice-x lattice-z -- point )
	| lattice-x lattice-z |
	lattice-x 7.31 * lattice-z 13.17 * + to seed
	seed hash-fraction 0.5 - 2 * corner-shift * lattice-x + hedge-spacing * land-origin-x + to x
	seed 0.37 + hash-fraction 0.5 - 2 * corner-shift * lattice-z + hedge-spacing * land-origin-z + to z
	[ x 0 z ] ;

\ a hash from 0 to 1 of the hedge from a corner to the next east (way 0) or north (way 1), different for each salt
: hedge-hash ( lattice-x lattice-z way salt -- fraction )
	| lattice-x lattice-z way salt |
	lattice-x 3.13 * lattice-z 5.71 * + way 0.53 * + salt + hash-fraction ;

\ whether a lattice line carries a lane: a line running east (way 0) by its place north, or north (way 1) by its place east
: lane-line? ( place way -- flag )
	| place way |
	place 7.7 * way 3.1 * + 1.3 + hash-fraction lane-share < ;

\ the fields' own colours, as aerial photographs of East Lothian, Fife and Renfrewshire show them (estimates read from the photographs): ploughed earth, dark and drier; stubble; ripe grain; grass dark, mid and light; young crops; rough grazing
0x5c4a3a constant ploughed-colour
0x7a6450 constant dry-ploughed-colour
0xb8a070 constant stubble-colour
0xc8a85a constant ripe-colour
0x46642e constant dark-grass-colour
0x587a36 constant grass-colour
0x6e8c42 constant light-grass-colour
0x7c9c4a constant young-crop-colour
0x8a8a60 constant rough-grazing-colour

\ the month the fields are coloured for, set by each flight; the kilometres built again when it changes
variable field-month
7 to field-month

: use-field-month ( month -- )
	| month ^field-month ^countryside-objects ^countryside-cell |
	month field-month = if exit then
	month to field-month
	{ } to countryside-objects
	[ null null ] to countryside-cell ;

\ the snow line for a flight; the kilometres built again when it changes
: use-snow-line ( height -- )
	| height ^snow-line ^countryside-objects ^countryside-cell |
	height snow-line = if exit then
	height to snow-line
	{ } to countryside-objects
	[ null null ] to countryside-cell ;

\ the shares of the fields in each colour in a month, in the arable east, browns and golds among the greens, or in the pastoral west, mostly grass, as [ colour share ] summing to 1: March and April ploughed and sown, May to July young crops and grass, August and September ripe grain and stubble, October to February stubble and the plough (estimates from the photographs and the farming year)
: field-crops ( month east -- crops )
	| month east |
	month 3 >= month 4 <= and if
		east if [ [ ploughed-colour 0.3 ] [ dry-ploughed-colour 0.15 ] [ grass-colour 0.25 ] [ dark-grass-colour 0.1 ] [ young-crop-colour 0.2 ] ]
		else [ [ grass-colour 0.4 ] [ dark-grass-colour 0.25 ] [ light-grass-colour 0.15 ] [ ploughed-colour 0.15 ] [ rough-grazing-colour 0.05 ] ] then exit
	then
	month 5 >= month 7 <= and if
		east if [ [ young-crop-colour 0.3 ] [ grass-colour 0.3 ] [ light-grass-colour 0.2 ] [ ploughed-colour 0.1 ] [ dark-grass-colour 0.1 ] ]
		else [ [ grass-colour 0.4 ] [ light-grass-colour 0.25 ] [ dark-grass-colour 0.2 ] [ young-crop-colour 0.1 ] [ rough-grazing-colour 0.05 ] ] then exit
	then
	month 8 >= month 9 <= and if
		east if [ [ ripe-colour 0.35 ] [ stubble-colour 0.15 ] [ grass-colour 0.3 ] [ dark-grass-colour 0.15 ] [ ploughed-colour 0.05 ] ]
		else [ [ grass-colour 0.4 ] [ dark-grass-colour 0.2 ] [ light-grass-colour 0.15 ] [ ripe-colour 0.15 ] [ rough-grazing-colour 0.1 ] ] then exit
	then
	east if [ [ stubble-colour 0.3 ] [ ploughed-colour 0.3 ] [ dry-ploughed-colour 0.1 ] [ grass-colour 0.2 ] [ dark-grass-colour 0.1 ] ]
	else [ [ grass-colour 0.4 ] [ dark-grass-colour 0.25 ] [ ploughed-colour 0.15 ] [ stubble-colour 0.1 ] [ rough-grazing-colour 0.1 ] ] then ;

\ whether the hedge on a field's west side (way 1) or south side (way 0) is missing, so the field joins its neighbour there
: hedge-missing? ( lattice-x lattice-z way -- flag )
	| lattice-x lattice-z way |
	way 0 = if lattice-z else lattice-x then way lane-line? if false exit then
	lattice-x lattice-z way 0 hedge-hash hedge-gap-share < ;

\ the colour of the field whose south-west corner is a corner of the lattice: where its west or south hedge is missing the colour of the field it joins, followed up to three times; then a crop picked by a hash from the month's shares, the east's or the west's by another hash weighed by how far east the field lies, wholly the west's 20 km west of 3.6°W and wholly the east's 20 km east of it
: field-colour-at ( lattice-x lattice-z -- colour )
	| lattice-x lattice-z |
	0 3 1 do step
		lattice-x lattice-z 1 hedge-missing? if
			lattice-x 1- to lattice-x
		else lattice-x lattice-z 0 hedge-missing? if
			lattice-z 1- to lattice-z
		then then
	loop
	lattice-x lattice-z hedge-corner first 20000 + 40000 / 0 1 clamp to east-share
	field-month lattice-x lattice-z 0 0.71 hedge-hash east-share < field-crops to crops
	lattice-x lattice-z 1 0.91 hedge-hash to pick
	crops last first to colour
	0 to reached
	0 crops size 1 do k
		reached crops k @i second + to reached
		pick reached < if crops k @i first to colour leave then
	loop
	colour ;

\ a lane along a hedge's line between two corners: two lines 3 m either side of it
: keep-lane-stretch ( sketch from onto coastal -- )
	| sketch from onto coastal |
	onto from v- to run
	[ run 2 @i negate 0 run first ] v-unit 3 v* to beside
	[ -1 1 ] ( way | sketch from beside way v* v+ onto beside way v* v+ coastal ground-line ) each ;

\ a line of trees along a hedge's line, one every 25 m, those not on water, their heights from 9 to 14 m by a hash
: keep-tree-line ( sketch from onto coastal seed -- )
	| sketch from onto coastal seed |
	onto from v- v-length 25 / round-down 1 max2 to n-trees
	0 n-trees 1 do k
		from onto k 0.5 + n-trees / v-between to base
		coastal if base first base 2 @i water-at? else false then not if
			sketch base seed k 1.7 * + hash-fraction 5 * 9 + sketch-tree
		then
	loop ;

\ the grid steps a kilometre's fields are cut into each way, and the radius of the sphere round them
4 constant fields-per-side
710 constant field-cell-radius

\ the surveyed grids' tiles by their centres' places, "x/z" to the tile, made on first use once the scenery is built
variable tiles-by-centre
null to tiles-by-centre

: tile-key ( x z -- key ) | x z | x round z round "{1}/{0}" format string>symbol ;

\ the grid tile a ground point lies on, or null: the first grid holding the point, the tile of 8 grid steps it falls in by the grid's own arithmetic, found by its centre; null too where that tile was all sea and left out. The fields and the towns' ground are drawn just after it
: tile-under ( x z -- tile )
	| x z ^tiles-by-centre |
	tiles-by-centre null? if
		{ } to tiles-by-centre
		terrain-tiles ( tile | tile@radius 2000 >= if tiles-by-centre tile tile@centre first tile@centre 2 @i tile-key ! drop then ) each
	then
	null to under
	0 terrain-grids size 1 do k
		terrain-grids k @i to grid
		under null? x z grid 0 near-grid? and if
			x grid@west - grid@spacing / 8 / round-down 8 * to tile-column
			z grid@south - grid@spacing / 8 / round-down 8 * to tile-row
			grid@west tile-column 4 + grid@spacing * + grid@south tile-row 4 + grid@spacing * + tile-key to key
			tiles-by-centre key has? if tiles-by-centre key @ to under then
		then
	loop
	under ;

\ the most a Norwegian field's corners differ in height, metres, about 6° across a field (an estimate): steeper ground is left to the forest
25 constant field-rise

\ whether a field's triangle stays: off the water, and in Norway on level farmland, its corners below the farmland's height and within a field's rise of each other
: field-triangle? ( corner-points coastal cover -- flag )
	| corner-points coastal cover |
	coastal if corner-points ( point | point first point 2 @i water-at? ) any? if false exit then then
	cover null? if true exit then
	corner-points ( point | point second ) map to heights
	heights heights first ' max2 reduce to highest
	highest farmland-height < highest heights heights first ' min2 reduce - field-rise < and ;

\ one kilometre's fields as a filled mesh: the 25 corners of its 16 fields lifted onto the ground, each field two triangles in its colour, a triangle left out where field-triangle? fails; in Norway a field white above the snow line; the colours with the mesh as :field-colours, the kilometre's centre and the tile it lies on; null when no field is left
: field-mesh ( first-x first-z coastal lift cones cover -- mesh )
	| first-x first-z coastal lift cones cover |
	fields-per-side 1+ to n-corners
	[ 0 n-corners 1 do b
		0 n-corners 1 do a
			first-x a + first-z b + hedge-corner to corner
			corner first to x
			corner 2 @i to z
			[ x lift if x z cones ground-height-under else 0 then z ]
		loop
	loop ] to points
	[ ] to triangles
	[ ] to colours
	0 fields-per-side 1 do b
		0 fields-per-side 1 do a
			b n-corners * a + to p00
			p00 1+ to p01
			p00 n-corners + to p10
			p10 1+ to p11
			first-x a + first-z b + field-colour-at to colour
			cover null? not if
				points p00 @i second snow-line >= if snow-colour to colour then
			then
			[ [ p00 p10 p11 ] [ p00 p11 p01 ] ] to pair
			0 2 1 do t
				pair t @i to triangle
				triangle ( corner | points corner @i ) map coastal cover field-triangle? if
					triangles triangle add-last! drop
					colours colour add-last! drop
				then
			loop
		loop
	loop
	triangles size 0 = if null exit then
	points triangles filled-mesh to mesh
	points 12 @i to middle
	mesh colours :field-colours ! middle :centre ! middle first middle 2 @i tile-under :tile ! ;

\ a kilometre's hedges from each of its sixteen corners east and north to the next: a lane where the line carries one, else a hedge or a line of trees or nothing, a hedge carrying a tree a third of the time
: keep-hedges ( hedges trees roads first-x first-z coastal -- )
	| hedges trees roads first-x first-z coastal |
	first-x first-x 4 + 1 do lattice-x
		first-z first-z 4 + 1 do lattice-z
			lattice-x lattice-z hedge-corner to corner
			0 2 1 do way
				way 0 = if lattice-x 1+ lattice-z else lattice-x lattice-z 1+ then hedge-corner to onward
				way 0 = if lattice-z else lattice-x then way lane-line? if
					roads corner onward coastal keep-lane-stretch
				else lattice-x lattice-z way 0 hedge-hash hedge-gap-share >= if
					lattice-x lattice-z way 0.29 hedge-hash tree-line-share < if
						trees corner onward coastal lattice-x lattice-z way 0.61 hedge-hash 100 * keep-tree-line
					else
						hedges corner onward coastal ground-line
						lattice-x lattice-z way 0.83 hedge-hash 0.35 < if
							corner onward lattice-x lattice-z way 0.47 hedge-hash v-between to base
							coastal if base first base 2 @i water-at? else false then not if
								trees base lattice-x lattice-z way 0.19 hedge-hash 6 * 8 + sketch-tree
							then
						then
					then
				then then
			loop
		loop
	loop ;

\ a Norwegian farmstead about a yard, as the photographs of Trøndelag show them: a white house of two storeys, 8 m by 14, and a red barn, 14 m by 30, 12 m to its ridge (sizes and colours estimates)
0xe4e0d4 constant farmhouse-colour
0x9a3428 constant barn-colour

\ one kilometre's countryside, { :objects :fields }. In Scotland its hedges, and three times in ten a farm, a house and a barn about a yard; in Norway no hedges, and six times in ten a farmstead where the yard lies on the farmland; each kind its own object, lifted onto the ground; and its fields filled. On water its ripples, eighty when the eye is near and low, else twelve, and no fields. In a town nothing
: cell-objects ( column row dense -- cell )
	| column row dense |
	land-origin-x column land-cell * + to west
	land-origin-z row land-cell * + to south
	west land-cell 2 / + south land-cell 2 / + water-at? if
		column row dense if 80 else 12 then ripples to waves
		{ :objects waves null? if [ ] else [ waves ] then :fields null } exit
	then
	west land-cell 2 / + south land-cell 2 / + clear-cell? if { :objects [ ] :fields null } exit then
	west land-cell 2 / + south land-cell 2 / + land-cover-at to cover
	column 7.31 * row 13.17 * + to seed
	west south coastal-cell? to coastal
	new-sketch to hedges
	new-sketch to trees
	new-sketch to roads
	new-sketch to farm
	new-sketch to barn
	column 4 * to first-x
	row 4 * to first-z
	cover null? if hedges trees roads first-x first-z coastal keep-hedges then
	first-x 1+ first-z 1+ hedge-corner [ 40 0 40 ] v+ to yard
	coastal if yard first yard 2 @i water-at? not else true then to dry-yard
	seed 90 * to farm-heading
	cover null? if
		seed 4.2 + hash-fraction 0.3 < dry-yard and if
			farm yard farm-heading 10 16 6 9 sketch-house
			farm yard farm-heading 25 0 0 placed farm-heading 12 24 7 10 sketch-house
			farm yard farm-heading 12 0 22 placed farm-heading 30 20 0 rectangle-corners sketch-loop
		then
	else
		seed 4.2 + hash-fraction 0.6 < dry-yard and yard first yard 2 @i ground-height farmland-height < and if
			farm yard farm-heading 8 14 6 9 sketch-house
			barn yard farm-heading 22 0 4 placed farm-heading 14 30 7 12 sketch-house
		then
	then
	west south cell-cones to lift to cones
	[ [ hedges hedge-colour ] [ trees tree-colour ] [ roads road-colour ]
	  [ farm cover null? if town-colour else farmhouse-colour then ] [ barn barn-colour ] ] to parts
	[ 0 parts size 1 do part
		parts part @i spread to colour to sketch
		sketch@edges size 0 > if
			lift if sketch cones lift-sketch then
			sketch colour sketch>object
		then
	loop ] to objects
	{ :objects objects :fields first-x first-z coastal lift cones cover field-mesh } ;

\ the most kilometres built in one frame, so crossing into a new kilometre spreads its building over a few frames
2 constant countryside-builds-per-frame

\ the near kilometres' field meshes gathered for culling and ordering: their centres and spheres, and the centres of the tiles they lie on, a field's own centre where it lies on no tile
: gather-fields ( meshes -- fields )
	| meshes |
	meshes size 0 = if { :meshes [ ] :centres 0 4 0-matrix :radii 0 1 0-matrix :tile-centres 0 4 0-matrix } exit then
	meshes ( mesh | mesh@centre spread 1 4 array ) map flatten meshes size 4 matrix to centres
	meshes ( mesh | mesh@tile null? if mesh@centre else mesh@tile@centre then spread 1 4 array ) map flatten meshes size 4 matrix to tile-centres
	meshes ( mesh | mesh :radius field-cell-radius @or ) map vector to radii
	{ :meshes meshes :centres centres :radii radii :tile-centres tile-centres } ;

\ the kilometres near a point: their objects and fields, built once each and kept, the nearest first, at most two a frame, those not yet built left out until a later frame builds them; the kilometres next to the point's own, while the point is below 400 m, in their dense form; gathered again each frame until all are built, then only when the point crosses into another kilometre or through 400 m
: refresh-countryside ( position -- )
	| position ^countryside-collection ^countryside-cell ^countryside-fields |
	position first land-origin-x - land-cell / round-down to column
	position 2 @i land-origin-z - land-cell / round-down to row
	position second 400 < to low
	countryside-cell [ column row low ] = if exit then
	0 to n-built
	true to complete
	[ ] to near-objects
	[ ] to near-fields
	0 countryside-reach 1+ 1 do ring
		column ring - column ring + 1+ 1 do c
			row ring - row ring + 1+ 1 do r
				c column - abs r row - abs max2 ring = if
					low c column - abs 1 <= and r row - abs 1 <= and to dense
					c r dense if "{1}/{0}/dense" else "{1}/{0}" then format string>symbol to key
					countryside-objects key has? not if
						n-built countryside-builds-per-frame < if
							countryside-objects c r dense cell-objects key ! drop
							++ n-built
						else
							false to complete
						then
					then
					countryside-objects key has? if
						countryside-objects key @ to cell
						near-objects cell@objects concat to near-objects
						cell@fields null? not if near-fields cell@fields add-last! drop then
					then
				then
			loop
		loop
	loop
	complete if [ column row low ] to countryside-cell then
	near-objects collect-objects to countryside-collection
	near-fields gather-fields to countryside-fields ;

\ a kilometre's fields' colours at a haze, a share of their own colour kept from 0 to 1 in sixteenths: each field's colour darkened by its slope's shade, faded into the sky; grey in a photograph; made once for each palette and haze and kept
: field-colours ( mesh haze -- colours )
	| mesh haze |
	haze 16 * round to level
	sky-colour level monochrome "{0}/{1}/{2}" format string>symbol to key
	mesh@colours key has? if mesh@colours key @ exit then
	level 16 / to light
	[ 0 mesh@shades size 1 do k
		mesh@field-colours k @i mesh@shades k @i dimmed sky-colour light blended
		monochrome if grey-of then
	loop ] to colours
	mesh@colours colours key ! drop
	colours ;

\ the visible meshes of a gathering of fields or towns' ground as items to draw in order of depth, [ depth :fields mesh ], each just nearer than the tile it lies on, so it is drawn over the tile and under what stands nearer; none at night, when the ground is dark and the towns blacked out
: ground-items ( gathered -- items )
	| gathered |
	stars-showing if [ ] exit then
	gathered@meshes to meshes
	meshes size 0 = if [ ] exit then
	gathered@centres gathered@radii visible-objects to shown
	shown num-elements 0 = if [ ] exit then
	gathered@tile-centres camera matmul 2 @j to depths
	[ 0 shown num-elements 1 do k
		shown k @e to index
		meshes index @i to mesh
		mesh@tile null? if 0 else mesh@tile ground-tile-reach then to reach
		[ depths index @e reach + 1 - mesh :sooner 0 @or - :fields mesh ]
	loop ] ;

\ a kilometre's fields, or a piece of a town's ground, drawn at their distance's haze
: draw-fields ( mesh -- )
	| mesh |
	mesh mesh mesh@centre eye@position v- v-length depth-light field-colours draw-filled-mesh ;

\ === the towns' ground ===

\ of each town's squares of built-up ground (its colour cities.telic's) a fifth darker blocks and a tenth paler streets and yards, the rest its own colour
0.2 constant dark-block-share
0.1 constant street-share
350 constant town-square

\ each town's built-up ground, [ key radius colour ]: the places the countryside leaves clear of fields, at the same reach, with Narvik's level centre
[ [ :edinburgh-castle 3500 edinburgh-colour ] [ :leith 1500 edinburgh-colour ] [ :glasgow-cathedral 4500 clydeside-colour ]
  [ :govan 2000 clydeside-colour ] [ :clydebank 1500 clydeside-colour ] [ :inverness-castle 2000 slate-colour ]
  [ :stirling-castle 1500 slate-colour ] [ :marischal-college 2500 aberdeen-colour ] [ :peterhead 1000 slate-colour ]
  [ :montrose 1000 slate-colour ] [ :kirkwall 1000 slate-colour ] [ :lerwick 800 slate-colour ]
  [ :nidaros 1500 timber-colour ] [ :narvik 800 timber-colour ] ] constant towns

\ how far a town's ground reaches at a bearing: between 85% and 110% of its radius, by a hash of the bearing's sixteenth, blended into the next
: town-reach ( radius seed angle -- reach )
	| radius seed angle |
	angle TAU / 16 * 16 + 16 mod to place
	place round-down to sector
	seed sector + hash-fraction seed sector 1+ 16 mod + hash-fraction place sector - * +
	seed sector + hash-fraction place sector - * - 0.25 * 0.85 + radius * ;

\ a square of ground of a size about a middle, two triangles at the ground's height in a colour, added to the piece of the grid tile under its middle, the pieces kept by their tiles' places
: add-square ( chunks middle-x middle-z side colour -- )
	| chunks middle-x middle-z side colour |
	middle-x middle-z tile-under to tile
	tile null? if :none else tile@centre first tile@centre 2 @i tile-key then to chunk-key
	chunks chunk-key has? not if chunks { :points [ ] :triangles [ ] :colours [ ] :tile tile } chunk-key ! drop then
	chunks chunk-key @ to chunk
	chunk@points size to base
	[ [ -0.5 -0.5 ] [ 0.5 -0.5 ] [ 0.5 0.5 ] [ -0.5 0.5 ] ] ( corner |
		middle-x corner first side * + to x
		middle-z corner second side * + to z
		chunk@points [ x x z ground-height z ] add-last! drop
	) each
	chunk@triangles [ base base 1+ base 2 + ] add-last! [ base base 2 + base 3 + ] add-last! drop
	chunk@colours colour add-last! colour add-last! drop ;

\ the share of the snow's light a Norwegian town's snowed roofs and streets keep, greyed by the chimneys and the traffic (an estimate)
0.82 constant town-snow-shade

\ a town's built-up ground as meshes, one for each grid tile it lies on: squares of 350 m on a grid about its point, those whose middles lie within the town's reach at their bearing, each two triangles at the ground's height, green in a park, else its colour, a darker block or a paler street by a hash; in Norway under snow down to the shore the parks white and the rest the snow greyed; a square with water at a corner or its middle cut into sixteen and those on water left out, so the rivers and the shore show; each mesh with its squares' colours, its middle, its tile and the radius round it
: town-pieces ( town -- pieces )
	| town |
	town spread to colour to radius to key
	key landmark-ground to centre
	centre first centre 2 @i land-cover-at null? not snow-line 0 <= and to snowed
	snowed if snow-colour town-snow-shade dimmed to colour then
	centre use-water-near
	centre first 0.013 * centre 2 @i 0.007 * + to seed
	radius 1.1 * town-square / round-up to reach
	{ } to chunks
	reach negate reach 1 do b
		reach negate reach 1 do a
			centre first a 0.5 + town-square * + to middle-x
			centre 2 @i b 0.5 + town-square * + to middle-z
			middle-x centre first - to east
			middle-z centre 2 @i - to north
			east north atan2 to bearing
			east sq north sq + sqrt radius seed bearing town-reach < if
				middle-x middle-z in-park? if
					snowed if snow-colour else grass-colour then
				else
					seed a 3.7 * + b 5.3 * + hash-fraction to pick
					pick dark-block-share < if colour 0.8 dimmed else pick dark-block-share street-share + < if colour 1.25 dimmed else colour then then
				then to square-colour
				[ [ 0 0 ] [ -0.5 -0.5 ] [ 0.5 -0.5 ] [ 0.5 0.5 ] [ -0.5 0.5 ] ]
				( place | middle-x place first town-square * + middle-z place second town-square * + water-at? ) any? if
					town-square 4 / to part
					0 4 1 do q
						0 4 1 do p
							middle-x p 1.5 - part * + to part-x
							middle-z q 1.5 - part * + to part-z
							part-x part-z water-at? not if chunks part-x part-z part square-colour add-square then
						loop
					loop
				else
					chunks middle-x middle-z town-square square-colour add-square
				then
			then
		loop
	loop
	[ 0 0 0 ] use-water-near
	chunks values ( chunk |
		chunk@points chunk@triangles filled-mesh to mesh
		chunk@points [ 0 0 0 ] ' v+ reduce 1 chunk@points size / v* to middle
		chunk@points ( point | point middle v- v-length ) map 0 ' max2 reduce to extent
		mesh chunk@colours :field-colours ! middle :centre ! chunk@tile :tile ! extent :radius !
	) map ;

\ the width of a city street the tenements line, between their fronts 15 m either side of its centre line, less a pavement's width each side
24 constant city-street-width

\ a town's roads' colour, street-colour-on its ground
: road-colour-in ( town -- colour ) 2 @i street-colour-on ;

\ the town a ground point lies in, or null: the first whose reach at the point's bearing takes it in
: town-at ( x z -- town )
	| x z |
	null to found
	0 towns size 1 do k
		towns k @i to town
		town first landmark-ground to centre
		x centre first - to east
		z centre 2 @i - to north
		east abs town second 1.1 * < north abs town second 1.1 * < and if
			east sq north sq + sqrt town second centre first 0.013 * centre 2 @i 0.007 * + east north atan2 town-reach < if
				town to found
				leave
			then
		then
	loop
	found ;

\ a line of [ x z ] points with points put in so no stretch is longer than a length
: split-line ( line length -- line' )
	| line length |
	[ line first
	  0 line size 1- 1 do k
		line k @i to from
		line k 1+ @i to onto
		onto first from first - sq onto second from second - sq + sqrt length / round-up 1 max2 to n-pieces
		1 n-pieces 1+ 1 do p from onto p n-pieces / v-between loop
	  loop ] ;

\ the towns' main roads as meshes, one for each grid tile they lie on, the city streets the tenements line among them, each line cut into stretches of 100 m or less so each stretch is drawn with the tile it lies on: each stretch of a road whose middle lies in a town and not on water a band of the road's width along it at the ground's height, two triangles, in its town's roads' colour; drawn just after the town's ground on the same tile
: road-pieces ( -- pieces )
	{ } to chunks
	[ glasgow-streets edinburgh-streets inverness-streets aberdeen-streets peterhead-streets montrose-streets
	  kirkwall-streets lerwick-streets trondheim-streets ] ( streets | streets values ) map [ ] ' concat reduce
	narvik-streets concat ( line | [ city-street-width line ] ) map town-roads concat to roads
	0 roads size 1 do r
		roads r @i spread 100 split-line to line to width
		width 2 / to half
		0 line size 1- 1 do k
			line k @i spread to start-z to start-x
			line k 1+ @i spread to end-z to end-x
			start-x end-x + 2 / to middle-x
			start-z end-z + 2 / to middle-z
			middle-x middle-z town-at to town
			town null? not if
				town first landmark-ground use-water-near
				middle-x middle-z water-at? not if
					end-x start-x - to dx
					end-z start-z - to dz
					dx sq dz sq + sqrt 1e-6 max2 to length
					dz negate length / half * to side-x
					dx length / half * to side-z
					middle-x middle-z tile-under to tile
					tile null? if :none else tile@centre first tile@centre 2 @i tile-key then to chunk-key
					chunks chunk-key has? not if chunks { :points [ ] :triangles [ ] :colours [ ] :tile tile } chunk-key ! drop then
					chunks chunk-key @ to chunk
					chunk@points size to base
					[ [ start-x side-x + start-z side-z + ] [ end-x side-x + end-z side-z + ]
					  [ end-x side-x - end-z side-z - ] [ start-x side-x - start-z side-z - ] ] ( corner |
						corner spread to z to x
						chunk@points [ x x z ground-height 0.5 + z ] add-last! drop
					) each
					chunk@triangles [ base base 1+ base 2 + ] add-last! [ base base 2 + base 3 + ] add-last! drop
					town road-colour-in to road-colour
					chunk@colours road-colour add-last! road-colour add-last! drop
				then
			then
		loop
	loop
	[ 0 0 0 ] use-water-near
	chunks values ( chunk |
		chunk@points chunk@triangles filled-mesh to mesh
		chunk@points [ 0 0 0 ] ' v+ reduce 1 chunk@points size / v* to middle
		chunk@points ( point | point middle v- v-length ) map 0 ' max2 reduce to extent
		mesh chunk@colours :field-colours ! middle :centre ! chunk@tile :tile ! extent :radius ! 0.5 :sooner !
	) map ;

\ every town's ground and main roads gathered for culling and ordering, built on the first flight and again when the snow line changes
variable town-grounds
null to town-grounds
variable town-grounds-snow-line
null to town-grounds-snow-line

: ensure-town-grounds ( -- )
	| ^town-grounds ^town-grounds-snow-line |
	town-grounds null? not town-grounds-snow-line snow-line = and if exit then
	snow-line to town-grounds-snow-line
	towns ( town | town town-pieces ) map [ ] ' concat reduce road-pieces concat gather-fields to town-grounds ;
